[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Axes the C actually branches on
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There are no compile-time `#ifdef`s, no global/runtime option setters, and no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m opaque handle to configure — the entire configuration space of this library is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m carried in the three arguments of the single entry point. The axes below are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m exactly the things the C source tests.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis 1 — `start_ptr` presence** (`if (start_ptr)` at line 43)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `NULL` → `start = 0` implicitly, and the `start > len` check is skipped
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - non-`NULL` → `start = *start_ptr`, range-checked
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis 2 — `stop_ptr` presence** (`if (stop_ptr)` at line 52)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `NULL` → `stop = len` (via a `size_t`→`int` truncating assignment), and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   *both* the `stop > len` and `stop <= start` checks are skipped
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - non-`NULL` → `stop = *stop_ptr`, range-checked twice
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Axes 1 × 2 give the four presence modes: `(NULL,NULL)`, `(set,NULL)`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `(NULL,set)`, `(set,set)`. These are genuinely different code paths, not just
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m different data.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis 3 — input string shape** (feeds `strlen`, and the `mystr + start`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m pointer arithmetic and `%.*s` in the final `printf`)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `len == 0` (empty string) — degenerate: makes `start`'s only valid value `0`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   and makes every `stop_ptr != NULL` an error
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `len == 1` — single element
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `len` many (short, and long enough to cross glibc's `printf` fast paths)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - byte content: pure ASCII; bytes with the high bit set (0x80–0xFF, i.e.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   non-UTF-8 — the C is byte-oriented and must **not** be validated as UTF-8 by
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   the Rust); bytes that are `printf` format metacharacters (`%`, `%n`, `%s`) —
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   these travel as *data* through the `%.*s` argument and must not be
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   reinterpreted; `\n`, `\t`, `\0`-adjacent and 0x7F control bytes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis 4 — index values within the valid range** (drives `stop - start` and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `mystr + start`)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `start == 0` (front)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `start` interior
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `start == len` (the maximum *valid* start: `start > len` is false, so a start
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   exactly at the terminator is accepted)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `stop == len` (maximum valid stop)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `stop == start + 1` (minimum valid width — `stop <= start` is rejected, so 1
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   is the narrowest slice)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - `stop - start` == full length
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Entry points
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There is exactly **one** public entry point, `slice`, and it *is* the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m lowest-level entry point — there are no convenience wrappers, no one-shot
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m helpers, and no internal functions with external linkage
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (`nm -D --defined-only` on the C `.so` lists only `slice`; see `SYMBOLS.md`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Every row below therefore calls `slice` directly through the `.so` export.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The observable output of `slice` is twofold and **both** are compared
